      "writtenOn": "2022-02-21T04:07:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is behavior change. It fix a bug that wifi p2p and ethernet tethering would not be supported if sb/wifi/bluetooth tethering are disabled. But it break the behavior the devices rely on disabling usb/wifi/bluetooth tethering to assume isTetheringSupported would return false. But they should use Settings.Global.TETHER_SUPPORTED Settings to disable the whole tethering instead of assuming isTetheringSupported would return false if some of tethering type is disabled.\n\nTwo options:\n1. In case, there is some devices in the field rely on this wrong behavior. Have a flag and let this change only apply after T. But this mean we end up two behavior. And we keep the wrong behavior before T even we think it is wrong...\n2. Still roll this out for R+ because it won\u0027t affect most devices because almost every device supports either hotspot or usb.\n\nI prefer option 2 because I think the impact is only for those device which don\u0027t support wifi,usb, bluetooth tethering and Settings.Global.TETHER_SUPPORTED don\u0027t set to false but these devices should not be too much.\n\nThis change may affect:\n1. test but TH is pass and we could be fixed it afterward. Some tests setup for OEM but they can fix it.\n2. If the device disable usb/wifi/bluetooth tethering:\n   before: Settings -\u003e no \"Hotspot \u0026 tethering\"\n   after : Settings -\u003e \"Hotspot \u0026 tethering\" -\u003e Ethernet tethering",
      "parentUuid": "f25d101f_0d6583e0",
      "revId": "48c7b6d5b80563918143ae42bcfa591b273e1b6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
