      "writtenOn": "2022-02-21T04:07:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, isAvailable could not be used to check whether ethernet tethering supported. It return true when there is tracking interface in EthernetFactory. So if ethernet tethering is enabled, there is no tracking interface in EthernetFactory and EthernetManager#isAvailable would return false.\n\nI think we always support ethernet tethering if ethernet is supported because there is no additional configuration inside tethering. If caller request ethernet tethering, tethering side always asking EthernetManager (if it is not null) and waiting callback to start ethernet tethering.\n\nSo checking whether EthernetManager is available is the existing behavior for whether support ethernet tethering",
